vacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nDesign decision record for the #2048 knowledge layer's multi-device sync cluster (issue #5838, parent programme #5678): `doc/2026-11-09_design_id5838.md`.\n\nDecisions recorded:\n\n- **Local-first** sync on ID's existing sync substrate (p2panda log sync + range sync, relays as availability only) — no second, knowledge-layer sync protocol; cloud-first rejected with reasons.\n- **Conflicts:** claims converge by #2048's observed-remove semantics; note bodies fork as sibling signed revisions with a deterministic default head and explicit merge revisions — no silent overwrite, no whole-object last-writer-wins; tombstone wins visibility over concurrent edits.\n- **Offline:** full read/write offline is the normal case; reconnect converges via the substrate's existing log/range method selection.\n- **E2EE tiered by the parent's ruled read-authority default** (public → signed cleartext; narrower-than-public → group-key encryption via p2panda-encryption, relays hold no keys), with relay metadata exposure stated honestly.\n- **Attachments/media:** content-addressed blobs via the blob gate, eager below threshold, lazy/on-demand above it; the open blob-gate-into-`serve` wiring (Phase 3 P3.4) is named as a dependency, not re-planned.\n\nParent compliance is explicit (§7): read-authority ruling and #2048 model consumed as-is, no divergences; programme verdict for the cluster is **adapt** (hosted tools' cloud-first sync rejected in §1).\n\n## Tests\n\nDocs-only change. The record was verified against the sources it reconciles with: parent issue #5678 (cluster statement + read-authority ruling), `doc/2026-11-01_design_id2048.md` (object model), the Phase 3 sync/relays record, the `/id-sync/1` ALPN-split and range/store-seam records, and the writer-set view projection record — all linked, none duplicated.\n